  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy. The key uncertainty is whether adding an image modality—particularly with a stronger encoder (ViT-L vs. the weak resnet50 that scored only 0.208)—can complement the strong RNA signal and push accuracy higher. Config_036 isolates this question by keeping the proven-best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and adding imagenet_vit_l with concat fusion. If it exceeds 0.650, the remaining 3 experiments can refine the multimodal direction (e.g., weighted fusion, transformer aggregation). If it does not, we confirm RNA-only dominance and can spend remaining budget on RNA-only refinements (e.g., config_006 transformer aggregation with scvi_n200). This is the highest-information experiment for the limited budget because it resolves the central question of whether multimodality adds value given the current evidence that image alone is very weak."
}

